SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  FILENAME= 'basebias.fits'                                                       NEXTEND =                    3                                                  TELESCOP= 'HST     '                                                            INSTRUME= 'STIS    '                                                            DETECTOR= 'CCD     '           / detector in use: CCD                           CCDAMP  = 'D       '                                                            CCDGAIN =                    1                                                  CCDOFFST=                    3                                                  OPT_ELEM= 'ANY     '                                                            APERTURE= 'ANY     '                                                            OBSTYPE = 'ANY     '                                                            BINAXIS1=                    1                                                  BINAXIS2=                    1                                                  FILETYPE= 'CCD BIAS IMAGE'                                                      PEDIGREE= 'INFLIGHT 28/04/2026 28/04/2026'                                      USEAFTER= 'Apr 28 2026 06:03:36'                                                DESCRIP = 'Weekly gain=1 bias for STIS CCD data taken after Apr 28 2026-------' TASKNAME= 'BASEJOIN'                                                            CHECKSUM= '8aT5ART52XT58XT5'   / HDU checksum updated 2026-08-13T12:54:50       DATASUM = '0       '           / data unit checksum updated 2026-08-13T12:54:50 COMMENT Reference file created by refstis.functions                             HISTORY Superbias image, combination of 9.0 input bias frames taken in          HISTORY CCDGAIN=1, BINAXIS1=1, BINAXIS2=1 mode.                                 HISTORY All input frames were from Proposal(s) 12345:                           HISTORY title                                                                   HISTORY The following input files were used:                                    HISTORY test1_raw.fits                                                          HISTORY test2_raw.fits                                                          HISTORY test3_raw.fits                                                          HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY The data were split into sub-lists of less than 30                      HISTORY imsets each. The script "refbias" was run on the                        HISTORY individual sub-lists and then averaged using the script                 HISTORY "refaver". The "refbias" procedure works as follows.                    HISTORY After joining the files together into a multi-imset                     HISTORY file, overscan subtraction is performed for every                       HISTORY individual bias frame. The bias frames in the multi-                    HISTORY imset file are then combined using ocrreject, which                     HISTORY performs a three-step iterative cosmic-ray rejection                    HISTORY with rejection thresholds of 5, 4, and 3 sigma,                         HISTORY respectively.                                                           HISTORY                                                                         HISTORY After cosmic ray rejection, the combined bias was                       HISTORY divided by the number of frames combined (ocrreject                     HISTORY adds images instead of averaging them), using the                       HISTORY stsdas.toolbox.imgtools.mstools.msarith routine.                        HISTORY Subsequently, hot pixels (and columns) were identified                  HISTORY as follows. A median-filtered version of the averaged                   HISTORY bias is created (kernel = 15 x 3 pixels) and                            HISTORY subtracted from the averaged bias, leaving a                            HISTORY "residual" image containing hot pixels and columns.                     HISTORY The pixels hotter than 5 sigma of the effective RMS                     HISTORY noise in the residual bias image are then identified,                   HISTORY and flagged as such in the Data Quality (DQ)                            HISTORY extension of the output reference bias file.                            END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     